column2:
Prosper, Indra, conqueror of enemies, Vritra-slayer, Pakashasana, god of gods, greatly fortunate, you have come to dwell on earth;
agnipuran:266:7	you are lord and eternal, devoted to the good of all beings, of infinite splendor, king, increaser of fame and victory;
agnipuran:266:8	may these gods increase your splendor, Indra, maker of good rain; Brahma, Vishnu, Maheshvara, Karttikeya, Vinayaka,
agnipuran:266:9	the Adityas, Vasus, Rudras, Sadhyas, Bhrigus, directions, hosts of Maruts, world-guardians, planets, Yakshas, mountains and rivers,
agnipuran:266:10	oceans, Shri, Earth, Gauri, Chandika and Sarasvati — may they increase your splendor. Victory, Indra, lord of Shachi!
agnipuran:266:11	By your victory always let good be recited for me; be pleased with kings, Brahmins and the subjects everywhere;
agnipuran:266:12	by your grace may the earth always be rich in crops; may there be welfare, without obstacle, and may calamities be greatly quieted.
